1
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:09,468
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

2
00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:11,303
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

3
00:00:11,345 --> 00:00:13,973
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

4
00:00:14,014 --> 00:00:19,770
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

5
00:00:19,812 --> 00:00:22,105
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

6
00:00:22,147 --> 00:00:24,733
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

7
00:00:24,775 --> 00:00:28,529
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

8
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:31,824
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

9
00:00:31,866 --> 00:00:33,701
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

10
00:00:33,742 --> 00:00:35,619
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

11
00:00:35,661 --> 00:00:38,831
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

12
00:00:38,873 --> 00:00:41,917
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

13
00:00:49,048 --> 00:00:51,552
SO, HONEY,
THIS, UH...

14
00:00:51,593 --> 00:00:54,513
THIS THREESOME
THING, UH

15
00:00:54,555 --> 00:00:57,182
I MEAN, HOW ARE WE EVEN GOING
TO START TO FIND...

16
00:00:57,224 --> 00:00:59,685
ACTUALLY, I'VE BEEN MAKING
A LIST OF ALL THE WOMEN I KNOW

17
00:00:59,727 --> 00:01:01,061
WHO MIGHT BE INTO DOING THIS.

18
00:01:02,730 --> 00:01:05,190
OH. WOW.

19
00:01:06,734 --> 00:01:08,109
HUH?

20
00:01:09,945 --> 00:01:11,279
BOY.

21
00:01:13,240 --> 00:01:15,367
WOW, SOMEONE'S BEEN
DOING THEIR HOMEWORK.

22
00:01:15,409 --> 00:01:17,160
YEAH.

23
00:01:17,202 --> 00:01:19,955
OH, AND I KNOW GAIL ROSTEN
IS IN THERE TWICE

24
00:01:19,997 --> 00:01:21,040
BUT SHE IS SO...

25
00:01:21,081 --> 00:01:22,750
OH, I KNOW.

26
00:01:24,418 --> 00:01:27,755
YOU KNOW, JUST, JUST
TALKING ABOUT IT IS...

27
00:01:27,796 --> 00:01:28,964
GETTING ME KIND OF...

28
00:01:29,006 --> 00:01:30,298
I KNOW, ME, TOO.

29
00:01:30,340 --> 00:01:31,299
YEAH?

30
00:01:31,341 --> 00:01:33,052
WELL, I THINK
BEN'S ASLEEP.

31
00:01:33,092 --> 00:01:35,054
OH, UM...

32
00:01:35,094 --> 00:01:38,515
YOU KNOW, I THINK
IT'LL BE BETTER

33
00:01:38,557 --> 00:01:40,893
IF WE JUST SAVE IT.

34
00:01:40,935 --> 00:01:41,936
YEAH.

35
00:01:43,771 --> 00:01:46,356
RIGHT. SAVE IT--
I CAN DO THAT.

36
00:01:47,608 --> 00:01:49,234
( karate yell )

37
00:01:55,365 --> 00:01:56,324
HEY, PHEEBS.

38
00:01:56,366 --> 00:01:57,451
HEY.

39
00:01:57,492 --> 00:01:58,577
HOW'S IT GOING?

40
00:01:58,619 --> 00:02:00,161
WELL, I GOT TO GET
OUT OF THIS BED!

41
00:02:00,203 --> 00:02:01,622
I'M GOING CRAZY HERE!

42
00:02:01,663 --> 00:02:02,998
CRAZY!

43
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:04,374
HERE YOU GO, SWEETIE.

44
00:02:04,416 --> 00:02:06,501
WHAT THE HELL IS THIS,
HERBAL TEA?

45
00:02:06,543 --> 00:02:07,669
I HATE HERBAL TEA.

46
00:02:07,711 --> 00:02:09,922
I PUT SOME HONEY IN IT.

47
00:02:09,964 --> 00:02:12,173
( mockingly ):
NYI, NYI, HONEY IN IT.

48
00:02:14,301 --> 00:02:16,344
SHE DOESN'T KNOW
SHE WAS FIRED YET, DOES SHE?

49
00:02:16,386 --> 00:02:18,097
NO. THE DOCTORS SAY
IT MAY KILL HER.

50
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:20,474
WHAT ARE YOU TWO GIRLS
WHISPERING ABOUT OVER THERE?

51
00:02:22,517 --> 00:02:24,519
BUT I THINK WE
SHOULD TELL HER.

52
00:02:30,025 --> 00:02:32,402
I MEAN, IT'S JUST SO REALISTIC.

53
00:02:32,444 --> 00:02:33,904
YEAH, I KNOW.

54
00:02:33,946 --> 00:02:36,031
YEAH. HIS NAME'S PAT.

55
00:02:36,073 --> 00:02:37,449
PAT THE DOG.

56
00:02:37,491 --> 00:02:40,327
OH! OH! I GET IT!

57
00:02:40,368 --> 00:02:41,703
( laughs )

58
00:02:41,745 --> 00:02:43,455
OH, GO...

59
00:02:45,624 --> 00:02:47,793
ARE YOU, UH, YOU...

60
00:02:47,835 --> 00:02:49,503
READY FOR A REFILL?

61
00:02:49,544 --> 00:02:51,964
OH, I PROBABLY SHOULDN'T.

62
00:02:52,006 --> 00:02:53,172
SO I WILL!

63
00:02:55,801 --> 00:02:58,720
OH... WOW.

64
00:02:58,762 --> 00:03:00,263
IT'S LIKE IT'S RAINING.

65
00:03:00,305 --> 00:03:01,765
PRETTY COOL, HUH?

66
00:03:01,807 --> 00:03:04,309
BUT IF YOU'RE THINKING YOU
COULD PUT A FISH IN THERE

67
00:03:04,351 --> 00:03:06,812
AND IT WOULDN'T GET SUCKED
UP INTO THE MECHANISM

68
00:03:06,854 --> 00:03:08,022
WELL, YOU'D BE WRONG.

69
00:03:09,356 --> 00:03:10,983
UM, CAN I USE YOUR BATHROOM?

70
00:03:11,025 --> 00:03:12,651
IT'S, UH, RIGHT
THROUGH THERE.

71
00:03:12,693 --> 00:03:13,652
OKAY.

72
00:03:13,694 --> 00:03:15,362
( sighs )

73
00:03:15,403 --> 00:03:17,238
YOU KNOW, I GOT TO TELL YOU

74
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:19,324
IF SOMEONE TOLD ME A WEEK AGO

75
00:03:19,366 --> 00:03:23,202
THAT I WOULD BE PEEING
IN JOEY TRIBIANNI'S APARTMENT...

76
00:03:23,244 --> 00:03:24,913
YEAH, LIFE'S PRETTY GREAT,
ISN'T IT?

77
00:03:27,166 --> 00:03:29,334
I HOPE YOU'RE HUNGRY.

78
00:03:29,376 --> 00:03:32,129
WE'RE STARTING
WITH OYSTERS.

79
00:03:32,171 --> 00:03:35,549
YOU KNOW WHAT THEY
SAY ABOUT OYSTERS,
DON'T YOU?

80
00:03:35,590 --> 00:03:37,676
THEY HAVE PARASITES?

81
00:03:38,927 --> 00:03:40,261
NO.

82
00:03:40,303 --> 00:03:43,348
UM, WELL, SOME PEOPLE
SAY THAT OYSTERS ARE...

83
00:03:43,390 --> 00:03:45,100
AN APHRODISIAC.

84
00:03:45,142 --> 00:03:47,061
WHAT PEOPLE?

85
00:03:47,102 --> 00:03:48,062
PEOPLE.

86
00:03:48,103 --> 00:03:50,689
PEOPLE SAY IT.

87
00:03:50,731 --> 00:03:52,607
COME HERE.

88
00:03:55,402 --> 00:03:57,029
SO, OYSTERS, HUH?

89
00:03:57,071 --> 00:03:58,572
( giggles )

90
00:03:58,613 --> 00:03:59,948
AND THEN WE'RE
GOING TO HAVE

91
00:03:59,990 --> 00:04:01,575
A LITTLE MIDDLE
EASTERN COUSCOUS.

92
00:04:01,616 --> 00:04:03,994
SOMETHING WE CAN EAT
WITH OUR HANDS.

93
00:04:04,036 --> 00:04:05,370
YOU KNOW, IT'S FUNNY

94
00:04:05,412 --> 00:04:07,831
WHEN WE WERE STUDYING
COMMUNICABLE DISEASES...

95
00:04:07,873 --> 00:04:10,084
NO, NO, NO, NO.

96
00:04:10,125 --> 00:04:11,418
IT'S SENSUAL.

97
00:04:11,459 --> 00:04:12,794
OH. DIDN'T KNOW.
OKAY.

98
00:04:12,836 --> 00:04:13,795
OKAY.

99
00:04:13,837 --> 00:04:15,881
( beeper sounding )

100
00:04:15,923 --> 00:04:17,091
OH, NO!

101
00:04:17,132 --> 00:04:19,676
I'M SORRY, SWEETIE,
IT'S THE HOSPITAL.

102
00:04:19,718 --> 00:04:22,221
THAT FOOD LOOKS GREAT.
MAYBE SAVE ME SOME?

103
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:24,681
I CAN'T PROMISE ANYTHING.

104
00:04:33,982 --> 00:04:36,651
WE'RE REALLY GOING
TO DO THIS, HUH?

105
00:04:37,945 --> 00:04:39,362
LOOKS LIKE IT.

106
00:04:39,404 --> 00:04:41,823
YOU KNOW, IF...
IF THIS IS TOO WEIRD FOR YOU

107
00:04:41,865 --> 00:04:43,825
YOU CAN STILL BACK OUT,
ANYTIME...

108
00:04:43,867 --> 00:04:45,493
( knocking on door )
I GOT IT.

109
00:04:45,535 --> 00:04:47,621
OKAY.

110
00:04:47,662 --> 00:04:49,206
SUSAN, HI.

111
00:04:49,248 --> 00:04:50,540
HEY.

112
00:04:51,583 --> 00:04:53,585
THANK YOU SO MUCH
FOR COMING.

113
00:04:53,627 --> 00:04:55,503
I WOULDN'T HAVE MISSED
IT FOR THE WORLD.

114
00:04:58,423 --> 00:04:59,674
I'M-I'M ROSS, BY THE WAY.

115
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:01,218
HELLO, ROSS.

116
00:05:03,053 --> 00:05:05,222
I LOVE WHAT YOU'VE
DONE WITH THIS SPACE.

117
00:05:05,264 --> 00:05:06,640
THANK YOU SO MUCH.

118
00:05:06,681 --> 00:05:08,391
( both giggling )

119
00:05:10,144 --> 00:05:12,729
HOW HOT IS THIS?!

120
00:05:17,442 --> 00:05:19,027
I'M SORRY YOU'RE HERE
WITH ME

121
00:05:19,069 --> 00:05:20,361
INSTEAD OF ROGER.

122
00:05:20,403 --> 00:05:21,571
YEAH, ME, TOO.

123
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:26,409
WELL, I COULD MAKE IT SEEM LIKE
HE'S HERE.

124
00:05:26,451 --> 00:05:29,537
HERE'S SOME LITTLE-KNOWN FACTS
ABOUT COUSCOUS:

125
00:05:30,580 --> 00:05:34,501
THEY DIDN'T ADD THE SECOND COUS
UNTIL 1979.

126
00:05:34,542 --> 00:05:37,254
( babbling )

127
00:05:37,296 --> 00:05:39,047
STOP IT! THAT'S NOT FUNNY.

128
00:05:39,089 --> 00:05:40,465
OKAY.

129
00:05:40,507 --> 00:05:42,009
I'M SORRY, OKAY.

130
00:05:42,050 --> 00:05:44,052
IT'S JUST, TONIGHT WAS
SUPPOSED TO BE, YOU KNOW...

131
00:05:44,094 --> 00:05:45,887
WELL, IT WAS SUPPOSED
TO BE A BIG DEAL.

132
00:05:45,929 --> 00:05:47,222
WHAT WAS TONIGHT?

133
00:05:47,264 --> 00:05:48,890
YOU DON'T WANT TO KNOW
WHAT TONIGHT WAS.

134
00:05:48,932 --> 00:05:49,933
OKAY.

135
00:05:51,268 --> 00:05:53,394
WHAT WAS TONIGHT?

136
00:05:55,147 --> 00:05:57,398
WELL, TONIGHT WAS...

137
00:05:57,440 --> 00:05:59,234
WAS GOING TO BE MY FIRST TIME.

138
00:05:59,276 --> 00:05:59,985
WITH ROGER?

139
00:06:01,903 --> 00:06:04,281
NOT JUST WITH ROGER?

140
00:06:05,115 --> 00:06:06,616
OH, MY GOD!

141
00:06:06,658 --> 00:06:09,577
ALL RIGHT, RELAX,
MR. I'VE-HAD-SEX-FOUR-TIMES!

142
00:06:12,122 --> 00:06:14,291
FOUR DIFFERENT WOMEN.

143
00:06:14,333 --> 00:06:16,751
I'VE HAD SEX WAY MORE TIMES.

144
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:18,003
HOW MANY?

145
00:06:18,045 --> 00:06:19,963
NINE.

146
00:06:21,380 --> 00:06:24,343
I WAS WAITING FOR
THE PERFECT GUY,
YOU KNOW.

147
00:06:24,383 --> 00:06:25,802
WELL, GOOD.
GOOD FOR YOU.

148
00:06:25,844 --> 00:06:28,805
YOU REALLY THINK
THAT ROGER IS THE PERFECT GUY?

149
00:06:28,847 --> 00:06:32,517
NO. HE'S NOT A HORRIBLE GUY.

150
00:06:32,559 --> 00:06:34,811
HEY, THAT'S WHAT I TELL GIRLS
ABOUT ME.

151
00:06:34,853 --> 00:06:37,939
CHANDLER, I'M GOING TO DIE
A VIRGIN!

152
00:06:37,981 --> 00:06:39,316
NO, YOU ARE NOT.

153
00:06:39,358 --> 00:06:40,817
YOU ARE SWEET AND WONDERFUL

154
00:06:40,859 --> 00:06:42,819
AND THIS IS GOING TO HAPPEN
FOR YOU.

155
00:06:42,861 --> 00:06:44,154
REALLY? WHEN?

156
00:06:44,196 --> 00:06:45,780
YOU WANT TO DO IT WITH ME?

157
00:06:45,822 --> 00:06:46,656
OKAY.

158
00:06:49,701 --> 00:06:51,995
I WAS KIDDING.

159
00:06:52,037 --> 00:06:54,789
SO WAS I.

160
00:07:00,170 --> 00:07:01,838
JOEY...

161
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:04,549
YOU'RE SUCH AN AMAZING ACTOR.

162
00:07:06,176 --> 00:07:10,597
HOW DO YOU KNOW WHERE
DR. DRAKE RAMORAY LEAVES OFF

163
00:07:10,638 --> 00:07:13,100
AND JOEY TRIBIANNI BEGINS?

164
00:07:13,141 --> 00:07:15,977
WELL, WITH DR. DRAKE

165
00:07:16,019 --> 00:07:18,813
THEY ALWAYS TELL ME WHAT TO SAY.

166
00:07:21,316 --> 00:07:26,154
AND WITH JOEY, I PRETTY MUCH
HAVE TO MAKE IT UP ON MY OWN.

167
00:07:26,196 --> 00:07:27,155
WOW.

168
00:07:27,197 --> 00:07:28,489
HMM.

169
00:07:28,531 --> 00:07:29,991
TELL ME SOMETHING, JOEY...

170
00:07:30,033 --> 00:07:31,034
WHOA!

171
00:07:31,076 --> 00:07:32,077
OH.

172
00:07:33,494 --> 00:07:35,705
I JUST FELL RIGHT OFF
THE COUCH THERE.

173
00:07:35,747 --> 00:07:36,790
YEAH, YOU DID.

174
00:07:36,831 --> 00:07:38,125
I'M OKAY.

175
00:07:38,166 --> 00:07:39,751
OKAY, HERE YOU GO.
WHOOPS.

176
00:07:39,793 --> 00:07:40,961
LET ME ASK YOU
A QUESTION.

177
00:07:41,002 --> 00:07:42,170
YEAH?

178
00:07:42,212 --> 00:07:45,299
WHEN WAS THE LAST TIME
SOMEONE TOLD YOU

179
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:47,592
JUST HOW BEAUTIFUL
YOU ARE?

180
00:07:47,634 --> 00:07:50,137
WOW.

181
00:07:50,178 --> 00:07:52,347
I CAN'T...
I CAN'T FEEL MY HANDS.

182
00:07:52,389 --> 00:07:55,267
OH, WELL, COME HERE.

183
00:07:58,270 --> 00:07:59,771
HMM?

184
00:07:59,813 --> 00:08:00,563
HUH?

185
00:08:00,605 --> 00:08:01,856
OH?

186
00:08:01,898 --> 00:08:02,899
OH?

187
00:08:16,455 --> 00:08:18,290
( retching )

188
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:26,840
WE CAN'T DO THIS.

189
00:08:26,881 --> 00:08:27,841
NO.

190
00:08:27,882 --> 00:08:29,176
( laughing )

191
00:08:29,217 --> 00:08:30,260
OYSTER?

192
00:08:30,302 --> 00:08:31,845
YEAH.

193
00:08:31,886 --> 00:08:34,681
OKAY, NOW, IF, IF,
IF WE DID DO THIS

194
00:08:34,722 --> 00:08:37,058
THERE'D BE A LOT OF PRESSURE
ON ME, YOU KNOW?

195
00:08:37,100 --> 00:08:39,602
BECAUSE YOU'VE BEEN WAITING
FOR A VERY LONG TIME

196
00:08:39,644 --> 00:08:41,646
AND I WOULDN'T WANT
TO DISAPPOINT YOU.

197
00:08:41,688 --> 00:08:44,024
YEAH, BUT SEE, I HAVE NOTHING
TO COMPARE IT TO.

198
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:46,360
SO EVEN IF YOU WERE HORRIBLE,
HOW WOULD I KNOW?

199
00:08:46,401 --> 00:08:49,863
I DO LIKE THAT.

200
00:08:49,904 --> 00:08:51,365
IT'S HARDER FOR ME--

201
00:08:51,406 --> 00:08:53,200
I'VE GOT THOSE FOUR OTHER WOMEN
TO COMPETE WITH.

202
00:08:53,241 --> 00:08:55,702
WELL, IF IT HELPS,
THERE WERE ONLY THREE.

203
00:08:57,371 --> 00:08:59,247
SO, IT WOULD JUST BE
FOR TONIGHT, RIGHT?

204
00:08:59,289 --> 00:09:01,249
ABSOLUTELY.
IT WOULD JUST BE ONE FRIEND

205
00:09:01,291 --> 00:09:02,750
HELPING OUT ANOTHER FRIEND.

206
00:09:02,792 --> 00:09:05,045
STOP IT. WE'RE NOT DOING THIS.

207
00:09:05,086 --> 00:09:06,338
LET'S DO IT.

208
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:07,506
NO. OKAY!

209
00:09:07,547 --> 00:09:08,756
OKAY!

210
00:09:10,091 --> 00:09:11,176
SO, UM...

211
00:09:11,218 --> 00:09:15,180
DO YOU HAVE ANY,
UH, MOVES?

212
00:09:16,890 --> 00:09:19,226
I HAVE SOME MOVES.

213
00:09:19,267 --> 00:09:20,977
I HAVE NO MOVES.

214
00:09:21,019 --> 00:09:22,437
OKAY.

215
00:09:23,813 --> 00:09:25,273
OKAY, WHAT YOU
DOING THERE?!

216
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:28,902
OH, YOU KNOW WHAT?
I'M SORRY, THIS IS
JUST TOO WEIRD.

217
00:09:28,943 --> 00:09:30,237
YEAH, LET'S
JUST FORGET IT.

218
00:09:30,278 --> 00:09:31,946
YEAH. WHAT IF I TURN OUT
THE LIGHTS?

219
00:09:31,988 --> 00:09:32,989
OKAY.

220
00:09:37,744 --> 00:09:40,038
Chandler:
OH, YEAH.

221
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,331
CHANDLER?

222
00:09:41,373 --> 00:09:44,334
( passionately ):
YEAH?

223
00:09:44,376 --> 00:09:46,545
THAT'S THE COUCH.

224
00:09:50,924 --> 00:09:52,926
OH, MY GOD.

225
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:55,636
I KNOW!

226
00:09:55,678 --> 00:09:57,556
I'LL TELL YOU SOMETHING--

227
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:59,933
WE ARE GOING
TO DO THAT AGAIN.

228
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:02,810
OH, OKAY!

229
00:10:02,852 --> 00:10:04,563
( laughs )

230
00:10:15,282 --> 00:10:16,616
MORNING.

231
00:10:18,159 --> 00:10:19,411
OH, RIGHT.

232
00:10:19,453 --> 00:10:20,912
YEAH.

233
00:10:20,954 --> 00:10:23,123
OH, GOD.

234
00:10:23,164 --> 00:10:24,707
OH, I CAN'T BELIEVE

235
00:10:24,749 --> 00:10:28,753
JOEY TRIBBIANI
HEARD ME THROW UP.

236
00:10:28,795 --> 00:10:31,506
YEAH, I MEAN, HE ACTUALLY
SAW YOU A LITTLE BIT, TOO.

237
00:10:31,548 --> 00:10:32,757
NO.

238
00:10:34,301 --> 00:10:36,595
OH, GOD, WE... HEY, WE...
WE DIDN'T, UM...

239
00:10:36,636 --> 00:10:38,388
NO, NO. NO.

240
00:10:38,430 --> 00:10:41,182
NOT AFTER SEEING THAT.

241
00:10:41,224 --> 00:10:45,019
GOD, I'M JUST A HORRIBLE PERSON.

242
00:10:45,061 --> 00:10:46,146
WHY?

243
00:10:46,187 --> 00:10:47,814
BECAUSE I'M MARRIED.

244
00:10:47,855 --> 00:10:49,899
THAT'S RIGHT--
I'M A MARRIED WOMAN

245
00:10:49,941 --> 00:10:51,443
AND I CAME TO A
TV STAR'S APARTMENT

246
00:10:51,485 --> 00:10:53,570
TO HAVE AN AFFAIR. UGH!

247
00:10:53,612 --> 00:10:56,114
THAT'S RIDICULOUS.

248
00:10:56,156 --> 00:10:58,908
I'M NOT A "STAR."

249
00:10:58,950 --> 00:11:03,079
I'M JUST A REGULAR FAMOUS ACTOR.

250
00:11:03,121 --> 00:11:07,250
YEAH, AND I'M A HORRIBLE,
HORRIBLE PERSON.

251
00:11:07,292 --> 00:11:10,086
RACHEL, WILL YOU
STOP SAYING THAT?

252
00:11:10,128 --> 00:11:11,338
HEY, HEY, LOOK...

253
00:11:11,379 --> 00:11:15,091
REMEMBER ON THE SHOW
WHEN CAPRI WAS DYING

254
00:11:15,133 --> 00:11:16,593
AND SHE GAVE ME...

255
00:11:16,635 --> 00:11:18,178
THE RING FROM
THE CAVE, YEAH.

256
00:11:18,219 --> 00:11:19,513
WOW. UH...

257
00:11:19,554 --> 00:11:22,182
OKAY, WELL... UH...

258
00:11:24,809 --> 00:11:25,935
( gasps )

259
00:11:25,977 --> 00:11:27,145
OH, MY GOD!

260
00:11:27,187 --> 00:11:29,063
THEY LET YOU KEEP
THAT STUFF?

261
00:11:29,105 --> 00:11:31,441
SURE. AS LONG AS
THEY DON'T FIND OUT

262
00:11:31,483 --> 00:11:33,485
YOU CAN KEEP
WHATEVER YOU WANT.

263
00:11:33,527 --> 00:11:35,487
AND I WANT YOU TO HAVE IT.

264
00:11:35,529 --> 00:11:37,405
NO, NO, NO, I COULDN'T.
YES, YES.

265
00:11:37,447 --> 00:11:39,491
AND EVERY TIME YOU LOOK AT IT

266
00:11:39,533 --> 00:11:43,119
I WANT YOU TO REMEMBER
THAT YOU... ARE A GOOD PERSON.

267
00:11:43,161 --> 00:11:45,455
OKAY, NOW, YOU HAD
THE CHANCE TO CHEAT--

268
00:11:45,497 --> 00:11:49,000
AND... WITH ME--

269
00:11:49,042 --> 00:11:50,377
BUT YOU DIDN'T

270
00:11:50,418 --> 00:11:53,712
AND THAT'S WHAT
THIS RING STANDS FOR.

271
00:11:53,754 --> 00:11:55,215
BUT I THOUGHT THAT RING

272
00:11:55,256 --> 00:11:57,800
STOOD FOR CAPRI'S
UNDYING LOVE HER BROTHER.

273
00:11:57,842 --> 00:11:58,968
YOU WANT THE RING OR NOT?

274
00:11:59,010 --> 00:12:00,345
YEAH.

275
00:12:05,684 --> 00:12:07,894
HEY, YOU'RE UP.
ALL RIGHT.
LOOK AT YOU.

276
00:12:07,935 --> 00:12:09,521
THOUGHT I'D TRY
TO TAKE A WALK.

277
00:12:09,563 --> 00:12:11,022
WILL YOU POUR ME
SOME WATER?

278
00:12:11,064 --> 00:12:12,440
I'LL BE BACK SOON.

279
00:12:12,482 --> 00:12:14,317
WHOA. YOU'RE NOT GOING
TO USE THE PAY PHONE

280
00:12:14,359 --> 00:12:15,360
TO CALL WORK, ARE YOU?

281
00:12:15,402 --> 00:12:17,529
NO. I'VE LEARNED
MY LESSON.

282
00:12:17,571 --> 00:12:18,863
OKAY.

283
00:12:18,905 --> 00:12:20,198
THANKS.

284
00:12:21,533 --> 00:12:22,617
LET'S GO.

285
00:12:22,659 --> 00:12:23,951
COME ON, MOVE IT.

286
00:12:23,993 --> 00:12:25,786
MOVE IT, PHOEBE, COME ON.

287
00:12:25,828 --> 00:12:27,205
SHOES, BRIEFCASE.

288
00:12:27,247 --> 00:12:30,041
THANKS, LOU. GOOD LUCK
WITH THE GALLBLADDER.

289
00:12:36,089 --> 00:12:38,258
HEY, JOEY, DID...

290
00:12:38,299 --> 00:12:40,510
DID YOU EVER HAVE
A THREESOME?

291
00:12:42,303 --> 00:12:43,388
UH... UH...

292
00:12:43,430 --> 00:12:45,181
LOOK, ROSS, I THINK
CAROL'S GREAT

293
00:12:45,223 --> 00:12:47,434
AND I'M SURE YOU'RE
A VERY ATTRACTIVE MAN

294
00:12:47,475 --> 00:12:49,936
BUT I...
NO.

295
00:12:49,977 --> 00:12:53,273
NO, THE REASON I'M
ASKING IS THAT...

296
00:12:53,314 --> 00:12:55,191
( laughs )

297
00:12:55,233 --> 00:12:57,151
I SORT OF HAD ONE
LAST NIGHT.

298
00:12:57,193 --> 00:12:59,153
YOU?
YEAH.

299
00:12:59,195 --> 00:13:00,530
WOW.
YEAH.

300
00:13:00,572 --> 00:13:03,199
ALL RIGHT, SO...
WAS IT AMAZING?

301
00:13:03,241 --> 00:13:04,867
IT WAS... IT WAS...

302
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:07,370
OKAY.

303
00:13:07,412 --> 00:13:10,331
JUST OKAY? DID YOU DO IT RIGHT?

304
00:13:10,373 --> 00:13:14,544
LOOK, IT'S JUST...
DID YOU EVER GO TO A PARTY

305
00:13:14,586 --> 00:13:19,798
AND THINK "WOULD ANYONE REALLY
MISS ME IF I WEREN'T HERE?"

306
00:13:20,883 --> 00:13:22,969
HUH.

307
00:13:23,010 --> 00:13:26,389
BUT STILL, ROSS...
YOUR WORST DAY WITH TWO WOMEN

308
00:13:26,431 --> 00:13:29,267
IS PRETTY MUCH BETTER
THAN ANY OTHER DAY.

309
00:13:29,309 --> 00:13:31,060
OH, OH, NO, ABSOLUTELY.

310
00:13:31,102 --> 00:13:32,604
( both laughing )

311
00:13:32,646 --> 00:13:34,481
YEAH.
YEAH.

312
00:13:36,524 --> 00:13:37,858
IT'S JUST...

313
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:40,654
MY PART SEEMED TO BE
OVER PRETTY QUICKLY

314
00:13:40,695 --> 00:13:42,363
AND THEN... AND THEN...

315
00:13:42,405 --> 00:13:44,407
THERE WAS A LOT
OF WAITING AROUND.

316
00:13:44,449 --> 00:13:46,075
OH.

317
00:13:46,117 --> 00:13:48,911
BUT YOU GOT TO BE
WITH BOTH OF THEM, RIGHT?

318
00:13:48,953 --> 00:13:52,290
NOT-NOT REALLY.

319
00:13:52,332 --> 00:13:54,375
IT WAS JUST CAROL.

320
00:13:54,417 --> 00:13:55,585
NOT THE OTHER ONE?

321
00:13:55,627 --> 00:13:58,421
NO, SHE KEPT
KICKING ME AWAY.

322
00:13:58,463 --> 00:14:00,590
OH. YEAH,
YOU DON'T WANT THAT.
NO.

323
00:14:00,632 --> 00:14:04,427
NO. WELL, HEY, AT LEAST
YOU GOT TO SEE A LOT OF STUFF.

324
00:14:04,469 --> 00:14:07,263
OH, I SAW A LOT
OF STUFF.

325
00:14:07,305 --> 00:14:09,015
YEAH.

326
00:14:09,056 --> 00:14:10,642
YOU GET A LITTLE BORED?

327
00:14:10,684 --> 00:14:12,310
A LITTLE.

328
00:14:12,352 --> 00:14:13,936
YEAH. MADE A SNACK.

329
00:14:13,978 --> 00:14:15,188
YEAH? WHAT...

330
00:14:15,229 --> 00:14:17,524
WHAT'D YOU HAVE?

331
00:14:17,565 --> 00:14:20,026
JUST A SANDWICH. YEAH.

332
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:21,528
TURKEY...

333
00:14:21,569 --> 00:14:22,862
A LITTLE MUSTARD.

334
00:14:22,903 --> 00:14:23,697
SOUNDS GOOD.

335
00:14:23,738 --> 00:14:25,072
IT REALLY WAS.

336
00:14:28,075 --> 00:14:29,703
HEY.

337
00:14:29,744 --> 00:14:31,788
HEY.

338
00:14:31,830 --> 00:14:35,834
LET ME TELL YOU ABOUT THIS CHICK
I SCORED WITH LAST NIGHT.

339
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:39,420
OH, NO, WAIT A MINUTE--
THAT WAS YOU.

340
00:14:39,462 --> 00:14:40,755
HEY, CHECK ME OUT.

341
00:14:40,797 --> 00:14:43,424
I'M A SLUT!

342
00:14:44,843 --> 00:14:47,303
SO YOU WANT TO DO SOMETHING
TONIGHT?

343
00:14:47,345 --> 00:14:49,930
OH, I CAN'T--
DR. ROGER'S COMING OVER AGAIN.

344
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:52,642
OH.

345
00:14:52,684 --> 00:14:55,228
OH, RIGHT, RIGHT,
BECAUSE YOU'RE STILL SEEING HIM

346
00:14:55,269 --> 00:14:56,563
AND, UH, HE'S A GOOD GUY.

347
00:14:56,604 --> 00:14:58,189
I MEAN, I REMEMBER A TIME...

348
00:14:58,231 --> 00:15:00,734
( snoring )

349
00:15:00,775 --> 00:15:02,402
ARE YOU OKAY?

350
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:04,320
( chuckling ):
YEAH. TOTALLY.

351
00:15:04,362 --> 00:15:05,572
TOTALLY. ARE YOU?

352
00:15:05,613 --> 00:15:07,615
GREAT. IT'S SO AMAZING.

353
00:15:07,657 --> 00:15:09,992
I MEAN, LAST TIME
DR. ROGER CAME OVER

354
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:11,118
I WAS SO NERVOUS

355
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:12,620
BUT THEN AFTER BEING WITH YOU

356
00:15:12,662 --> 00:15:15,582
I'M ALL, LIKE,
"CAN THE DOCTOR SEE ME NOW?"

357
00:15:15,623 --> 00:15:17,458
I'LL BET HE CAN.

358
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:19,753
"YOU KNOW, I DON'T HAVE
AN APPOINTMENT

359
00:15:19,794 --> 00:15:21,629
BUT I SURE COULD USE
A PHYSICAL."

360
00:15:21,671 --> 00:15:24,298
( chuckling )

361
00:15:24,340 --> 00:15:26,634
ARE YOU SURE YOU'RE OKAY?

362
00:15:26,676 --> 00:15:29,095
OH, YEAH. DON'T WORRY ABOUT ME--
I'LL BE FINE.

363
00:15:29,136 --> 00:15:30,638
( karate yell )

364
00:15:37,395 --> 00:15:38,813
( gasps ):
OH!

365
00:15:40,815 --> 00:15:42,483
MY GOD... BARRY!

366
00:15:42,525 --> 00:15:44,736
Y-YOU SAID YOU WERE GOING
TO BE AWAY ALL WEEKEND.

367
00:15:44,778 --> 00:15:46,987
OH. THAT'S RIGHT.

368
00:15:47,029 --> 00:15:48,989
I'M SORRY. I AM EARLY.

369
00:15:49,031 --> 00:15:51,033
FINISH, PLEASE!

370
00:15:56,955 --> 00:16:00,543
SURPRISE. LOOK WHO'S BACK.

371
00:16:00,585 --> 00:16:02,420
HEY, PHEEBS.
HEY.

372
00:16:02,462 --> 00:16:04,130
CALL SECURITY.

373
00:16:04,171 --> 00:16:07,258
PHEEBS, UH,
DIDN'T YOU GET FIRED?

374
00:16:07,300 --> 00:16:08,760
I DON'T THINK SO.

375
00:16:08,802 --> 00:16:10,177
PHOEBE?

376
00:16:10,219 --> 00:16:12,931
JACK! HEY.
HEY.

377
00:16:12,972 --> 00:16:14,098
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

378
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:15,683
ALL BETTER. BACK TO WORK.

379
00:16:15,725 --> 00:16:18,269
EXCEPT THIS CLOWN FROM RESEARCH
TOLD ME I WAS FIRED.

380
00:16:18,311 --> 00:16:20,521
HE SHOULD DO HIS
RESEARCH, HUH?

381
00:16:20,563 --> 00:16:23,775
WELL, YOU WERE FIRED.

382
00:16:23,817 --> 00:16:26,277
NUH-UH.

383
00:16:26,319 --> 00:16:28,529
I TOLD THAT GUY
WHO ANSWERED YOUR PHONE.

384
00:16:28,571 --> 00:16:30,448
OH. OKAY,
I DIDN'T GET THAT MESSAGE

385
00:16:30,490 --> 00:16:31,908
SO THIS DOESN'T COUNT.

386
00:16:31,950 --> 00:16:33,868
ANYWAY, I'LL BE IN MY OFFICE.

387
00:16:33,910 --> 00:16:36,830
UH, PHOEBE, I... YOU-YOU
DON'T HAVE AN OFFICE.

388
00:16:36,871 --> 00:16:39,290
THAT'S ALL RIGHT--
I'LL-I'LL WORK RIGHT HERE.

389
00:16:39,332 --> 00:16:41,960
THIS IS GOOD.
NEXT TO THIS PLANT.

390
00:16:42,001 --> 00:16:43,920
PHOEBE, LET'S NOT
MAKE A SCENE.

391
00:16:43,962 --> 00:16:45,880
YOU'RE IN MY OFFICE.

392
00:16:45,922 --> 00:16:47,423
LOOK...

393
00:16:47,465 --> 00:16:50,134
I HAVE MADE A LOT OF CASH
FOR THIS COMPANY, OKAY?

394
00:16:50,176 --> 00:16:53,095
I AM TALKING BIG BUCKS--
PESOS, YEN, RUBLES.

395
00:16:53,137 --> 00:16:55,222
YOU MAKE ONE LITTLE MISTAKE...

396
00:16:55,264 --> 00:16:57,391
YOU LOST $13 MILLION.

397
00:16:57,433 --> 00:16:59,519
OH, SO NOW THIS IS
ALL ABOUT MONEY?

398
00:16:59,560 --> 00:17:01,020
YOU KNOW

399
00:17:01,061 --> 00:17:03,189
IT'S BAD ENOUGH THAT... OW.

400
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:05,399
OH, YOU HAVE GOT TO BE KIDDING.

401
00:17:05,441 --> 00:17:06,943
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?

402
00:17:06,985 --> 00:17:09,487
I'M HAVING ANOTHER
HEART ATTACK.
WHAT?

403
00:17:09,529 --> 00:17:12,072
I'M HAVING ANOTHER HEART ATTACK!

404
00:17:12,114 --> 00:17:13,491
CALL 9-1-1!

405
00:17:13,533 --> 00:17:14,659
TAKE IT EASY, NOW.

406
00:17:14,701 --> 00:17:15,827
DUMB-ASS!

407
00:17:18,245 --> 00:17:19,330
HEY, PHEEBS.

408
00:17:19,372 --> 00:17:20,498
HOW'S IT GOING?

409
00:17:20,540 --> 00:17:21,582
THEY FIRED ME

410
00:17:21,624 --> 00:17:23,125
AND I'M HAVING A HEART ATTACK.

411
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:25,211
OH. WELL,
WELCOME BACK.
YEAH.

412
00:17:28,882 --> 00:17:30,383
HI, ROSS.
HI, RACHEL.

413
00:17:30,424 --> 00:17:32,092
IS JOEY TRIBIANNI HERE?

414
00:17:32,134 --> 00:17:33,761
UM... NO.

415
00:17:33,803 --> 00:17:35,179
WELL, IF YOU SEE HIM

416
00:17:35,221 --> 00:17:37,807
WILL YOU PLEASE TELL HIM
THAT I'M LOOKING FOR HIM

417
00:17:37,849 --> 00:17:40,685
AND THAT THIS TIME, I AM
NOT GOING TO THROW UP!

418
00:17:42,436 --> 00:17:43,771
ARE YOU OKAY?

419
00:17:43,813 --> 00:17:45,481
ME? I'M GREAT.

420
00:17:45,523 --> 00:17:48,484
I'M FINE. I'M SO GOOD.

421
00:17:48,526 --> 00:17:51,153
BUT... YOU KNOW
WHO'S NOT GREAT?

422
00:17:51,195 --> 00:17:52,238
MEN.

423
00:17:52,279 --> 00:17:53,698
YOU'RE A MAN, RIGHT, ROSS?

424
00:17:53,740 --> 00:17:55,033
YEAH.
SIT DOWN.

425
00:17:55,073 --> 00:17:56,367
OKAY.

426
00:17:56,409 --> 00:17:59,412
LET ME, UH...
LET ME ASK YOU SOMETHING.

427
00:17:59,453 --> 00:18:03,917
DO WEDDING VOWS MEAN SQUAT
TO YOU PEOPLE?

428
00:18:05,418 --> 00:18:07,712
AND WHY IS IT THAT
THE SECOND WE TELL YOU

429
00:18:07,754 --> 00:18:10,673
WE ARE GOING OUT OF TOWN,
BAM, THERE YOU ARE IN BED

430
00:18:10,715 --> 00:18:12,675
WITH THE NEIGHBOR'S DOG-WALKER?!

431
00:18:15,177 --> 00:18:17,764
WE'RE SORRY.

432
00:18:17,805 --> 00:18:19,974
NO, SERIOUSLY. SERIOUSLY.

433
00:18:20,016 --> 00:18:23,394
WHAT HAS HAPPENED
TO THE SANCTITY OF MARRIAGE?

434
00:18:23,436 --> 00:18:26,522
DIDN'T YOU SPEND
LAST NIGHT AT JOEY'S?

435
00:18:26,564 --> 00:18:28,524
OH, WHAT ARE YOU, A DETECTIVE?

436
00:18:30,944 --> 00:18:34,072
LOOK, I DON'T KNOW WHAT'S GOING
ON WITH YOU AND YOUR HUSBAND

437
00:18:34,113 --> 00:18:36,490
AND WHAT IS HOPEFULLY
AN ADULT DOG-WALKER...

438
00:18:38,576 --> 00:18:39,869
LOOK, CAN I JUST SAY

439
00:18:39,911 --> 00:18:41,454
NOT ALL MEN ARE LIKE THAT.

440
00:18:41,495 --> 00:18:42,329
OH...
HEY...

441
00:18:42,371 --> 00:18:43,539
THERE ARE SOME MEN

442
00:18:43,581 --> 00:18:44,707
WHO WILL DO
WHATEVER IT TAKES

443
00:18:44,749 --> 00:18:45,792
TO MAKE THEIR
MARRIAGE WORK.

444
00:18:45,833 --> 00:18:47,752
'KAY, THERE ARE SOME MEN

445
00:18:47,794 --> 00:18:50,421
WHO WILL STAND BY AND
WATCH AS THEIR WIVES

446
00:18:50,463 --> 00:18:53,758
ENGAGE IN WHAT CAN ONLY BE
DESCRIBED AS A TWOSOME...

447
00:18:53,800 --> 00:18:57,053
WITH-WITH SOME WOMAN SHE
BARELY KNOWS FROM THE GYM.

448
00:18:58,054 --> 00:19:00,264
WHO ARE THESE MEN?

449
00:19:00,306 --> 00:19:01,557
JUST-JUST MEN.

450
00:19:01,599 --> 00:19:02,850
A GUY I KNOW.

451
00:19:02,892 --> 00:19:04,560
WELL, YOU MIGHT
WANT TO TELL HIM

452
00:19:04,602 --> 00:19:09,148
IT SOUNDS LIKE
HIS WIFE... IS GAY.

453
00:19:09,189 --> 00:19:10,900
SHE IS NOT...

454
00:19:15,446 --> 00:19:17,490
SHE'S GAY.

455
00:19:20,158 --> 00:19:22,161
OH, MY GOD.

456
00:19:23,496 --> 00:19:26,124
SHE IS SO GAY!

457
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:32,005
I CAN'T BELIEVE THIS.

458
00:19:32,046 --> 00:19:35,257
GOOD DAY FOR MARRIED
PEOPLE, HUH?

459
00:19:37,135 --> 00:19:39,929
I'M SORRY YOUR HUSBAND
CHEATED ON YOU.

460
00:19:39,971 --> 00:19:42,682
I'M SORRY YOUR WIFE IS GAY.

461
00:19:44,475 --> 00:19:46,853
I GUESS WOMEN AREN'T
THAT GREAT, EITHER, HUH?

462
00:19:46,894 --> 00:19:48,896
TRY TELLING MY WIFE THAT.

463
00:19:53,693 --> 00:19:55,736
OKAY TO COME IN?

464
00:19:55,778 --> 00:19:58,197
YEAH, COME IN, EAT,
WHATEVER YOU WANT.

465
00:19:58,238 --> 00:20:00,366
DR. ROGER GOT BEEPED AGAIN.

466
00:20:00,407 --> 00:20:03,077
YEAH, I KNOW.
GUESS WHO BEEPED HIM.

467
00:20:04,453 --> 00:20:05,746
WHAT?

468
00:20:05,788 --> 00:20:07,081
I'M THE RUPTURED SPLEEN.

469
00:20:07,123 --> 00:20:08,541
( laughs )

470
00:20:08,582 --> 00:20:11,335
WHY WOULD YOU DO THAT?

471
00:20:11,377 --> 00:20:14,672
BECAUSE YOU SHOULDN'T
BE WITH HIM.

472
00:20:14,714 --> 00:20:16,924
YOU...

473
00:20:16,966 --> 00:20:18,759
YOU SHOULD BE WITH ME.

474
00:20:20,928 --> 00:20:22,180
REALLY?

475
00:20:22,221 --> 00:20:24,348
YEAH. WHEN YOU WERE
TALKING ABOUT ROGER

476
00:20:24,390 --> 00:20:25,975
THAT WAS KILLING ME. LOOK...

477
00:20:26,017 --> 00:20:27,226
THINGS LIKE LAST NIGHT

478
00:20:27,267 --> 00:20:28,853
THEY DON'T JUST HAPPEN,
YOU KNOW

479
00:20:28,895 --> 00:20:30,312
OR AT LEAST NOT TO ME.

480
00:20:30,354 --> 00:20:32,857
AND WITH THE OTHER TWO WOMEN...

481
00:20:34,817 --> 00:20:36,903
IN THE MORNING, YOU KNOW,
I WOULD JUST LIE THERE

482
00:20:36,944 --> 00:20:39,405
AND I COULDN'T WAIT TO JUST
GO HANG OUT WITH MY FRIENDS

483
00:20:39,446 --> 00:20:43,076
BUT WITH YOU...

484
00:20:43,117 --> 00:20:46,412
I WAS, YOU KNOW,
ALREADY WITH A FRIEND.

485
00:20:46,453 --> 00:20:48,206
CHANDLER...

486
00:20:48,246 --> 00:20:51,084
I KNOW YOU PROBABLY DON'T WANT
TO GO OUT WITH ME, YOU KNOW

487
00:20:51,125 --> 00:20:52,626
'CAUSE I MAKE TOO MANY JOKES

488
00:20:52,668 --> 00:20:55,088
AND I'VE NEVER BEEN
IN A SERIOUS RELATIONSHIP

489
00:20:55,129 --> 00:20:57,590
AND I GUESS I'M NOT
TECHNICALLY A "DOCTOR."

490
00:21:05,431 --> 00:21:07,934
THERE WAS JUST ONE
WOMAN, WASN'T THERE?

491
00:21:07,975 --> 00:21:09,393
NO, THERE WERE TWO.

492
00:21:09,435 --> 00:21:11,187
INCLUDING ME?
OH, YEAH.

493
00:21:18,945 --> 00:21:20,654
♪ IT ONLY TAKES
TWO HEART ATTACKS ♪

494
00:21:20,696 --> 00:21:22,448
♪ TO FINALLY MAKE YOU SEE ♪

495
00:21:22,489 --> 00:21:24,366
♪ ONE OF THEM WON'T DO IT ♪

496
00:21:24,408 --> 00:21:27,745
♪ BUT THE SECOND'LL
SET YOU FREE ♪

497
00:21:30,164 --> 00:21:32,332
